  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syria Education Programme II (SEP II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEP-II will deliver the UK&#x2019;s commitment to girls&#x2019; education and aims to enhance equitability of education  for girls and boys by strengthening the quality and inclusivity of formal primary  education in Northwest Syria. It will achieve this by focusing on four key areas: (i) Strengthening local education systems so that they are accountable, effective, and responsive (ii) Enhancing school level capacity to deliver inclusive, gender responsive and quality learning, (iii) Developing effective systems to support inclusion, mental health &amp; child protection, and (iv) Generating more predictable financing for sector implementation, including teacher salaries.</narrative>
  </description>
